<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>

    <!-- The strip along the bottom of the player that never accepts a touch,
         not even while the overlay has been lifted.

         What it covers is everything below YouTube's seek bar. The embed draws
         its control row inset from the bottom edge, so under the bar there is
         a band that belongs to nothing useful — and a scrub that drifts
         downward off the bar lands there, on whatever the player puts under
         it, or on the system's back/home gesture.

         This is a constant because it has to be. The player is a cross-origin
         iframe: its DOM cannot be read, so there is no way to ask where the
         bar actually is. The number is the inset YouTube's mobile embed
         currently uses, and it is the one value in the player that depends on
         somebody else's layout — if a future embed moves its controls, this is
         what needs revisiting. Erring small on purpose: too tall and it eats
         the seek bar, which is the one control the reveal exists to reach. -->
    <dimen name="player_bottom_block">16dp</dimen>

</resources>
